# Parity tooling output. The four tools that produce parity evidence -
# test/parity/manifest.js, capture.js, replay.js and joi-matrix.js - take their
# destination from --out (or from the PARITY_ARTIFACT_DIR directory) and have no
# repository default, so nothing below is written unless a run was pointed at
# the worktree on purpose. The two documentation generators, error-edges.js and
# convert-inventory.js, still default to the docs/*.md deliverables they exist
# to produce, which are tracked on purpose and are not listed here. What is
# listed is the two kinds of file that a run inside the worktree still leaves
# behind: the temporary file each tool renames its artifact from, which survives
# only a killed process, and the replay and comparison outputs, which are run
# results rather than evidence. The committed
# artifacts are deliberately NOT listed: test/parity/route-manifest.json,
# route-table.json, corpus.json and joi-baseline.json (with their provenance
# sidecars) are reviewable deliverables and must stay committable.
*.parity-tmp-*
test/parity/replay-result.json
test/parity/replay-result.json.provenance.json
test/parity/replay-report.txt
test/parity/joi-comparison.json
test/parity/joi-comparison.json.target.json
test/parity/joi-comparison.json.provenance.json

